Dear Ms Cridland,

I attach a letter concerning the decisions being made about my attendance a=
nd my return to duty, and the handling of my personal information.

I would be grateful if your office would bring it to your personal attentio=
n: it is a disclosure under section 89 of the Public Sector Act 2022, which=
 the Act directs to the chief executive.

I have addressed it to you because section 89 of the Public Sector Act 2022=
 makes the chief
executive the person to whom a conflict is disclosed, and the only person w=
ho may authorise an officer to continue to act in a matter affected by one.=
 I do not raise it with you to escalate it.

I make no allegation against any individual and I ask for no finding to be =
made about anyone.
The letter asks five questions and proposes the ordinary separation of func=
tions. If the answers
show the matter has been dealt with, that will resolve it and I will take i=
t no further.

Kind regards,
Cory Shepherd
AO3, Switchboard Services, Logan Hospital
0417 400 227



